+# FTS Full-Text Search — Contract
+
+## Setup & Constraints
+
+| Criterion | Verification |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| The project uses `better-sqlite3` with WAL mode, foreign keys ON | `test/notes.test.ts` passes |
+| FTS5 is the full-text search engine | FTS5 virtual table created in `createDatabase()` |
+| No new dependencies beyond `better-sqlite3` (FTS5 is built-in) | `package.json` unchanged |
+| All 15 existing CRUD tests continue to pass | `npm test` — notes CRUD tests |
+| All 20 search tests pass | `npm test` — search tests |
+
+## Requirement 1: Search Endpoint (`GET /notes/search?q=<query>`)
+
+| # | Criterion | Verification |
+|---|-----------|-------------|
+| 1.1 | Endpoint returns 200 and matching results for a keyword | Test 1: `?q=python` → `res.body.results.length > 0` |
+| 1.2 | Results include `snippet` field | Test 2: `res.body.results[0].snippet` is a string |
+| 1.3 | Snippet contains `<mark>` tags around matched terms | Test 3: `snippet.includes('<mark>') && snippet.includes('</mark>')` |
+| 1.4 | Results ranked by BM25 (ascending rank = more relevant) | Test 4: `results[i].rank >= results[i-1].rank` for query `programming` |
+| 1.5 | Quoted phrase search works (`?q="exact phrase"`) | Test 5: `?q="chocolate chip"` → result titles include "chocolate" |
+| 1.6 | Each result has `id` (number), `title` (string), `snippet` (string), `rank` (number) | Test 6: all 4 fields present with correct types |
+| 1.7 | Non-matching query returns empty `results` array | Test 7: `?q=xyznonexistentterm` → `results === []` |
+| 1.8 | Missing `q` parameter returns 400 | Test 8: `?q=` (absent) → status 400 |
+| 1.9 | Empty `q=` returns 400 | Test 9: `?q=` (empty) → status 400 |
+| 1.10 | Pagination: page=1 returns ≤20 results, has page/perPage fields | Test 10: `?q=the&page=1` → `len <= 20`, `page === 1`, `perPage === 20` |
+| 1.11 | Pagination: page=2 returns next page | Test 11: `?q=the&page=2` → `page === 2`, `results` is array |
+| 1.12 | Response includes `total` count | Test 12: `?q=programming` → `res.body.total` is number > 0 |
+| 1.13 | Special characters in query don't crash (returns 200 + results array) | Test 19: `hello%20world`, `test%26test`, `it%27s`, `%3Cscript%3E`, `foo%2Bbar`, `a%2Fb` |
+| 1.14 | Response time under 100ms for seeded dataset | Test 20: `?q=programming` → `elapsed < 100ms` |
+
+## Requirement 2: Suggest Endpoint (`GET /notes/search/suggest?q=<prefix>`)
+
+| # | Criterion | Verification |
+|---|-----------|-------------|
+| 2.1 | Suggest returns up to 5 results for a valid prefix | Test 13: `?q=learn` → `len <= 5`, `len > 0` |
+| 2.2 | Suggest results match prefix against note content | Test 14: `?q=getting` → result titles include "Getting Started with TypeScript" |
+| 2.3 | Suggest results have `id` and `title` fields (`SuggestResult`) | Test 13/14: object shape verification |
+| 2.4 | Empty `q=` returns 400 | Test 15: `?q=` → status 400 |
+
+## Requirement 3: FTS Index Synchronization
+
+| # | Criterion | Verification |
+|---|-----------|-------------|
+| 3.1 | New note appears in FTS search immediately after create | Test 16: POST with unique term → search finds it |
+| 3.2 | Updated note content reflected in FTS search | Test 17: Update body with unique term → search finds new, old term gone |
+| 3.3 | Deleted note disappears from FTS search | Test 18: Create → verify in search → delete → verify gone |
+| 3.4 | Triggers or manual sync used (not periodic reindex) | Trigger-based approach in `createDatabase()` |
+
+## Response Format Verification
+
+- Search: `res.body` shape = `{ results: SearchResult[], total: number, page: number, perPage: number }`
+- Suggest: `res.body` shape = `{ results: SuggestResult[] }`
+- Error (400): `{ error: string }` with status 400
+
+## Route Ordering
+
+- `GET /notes/search` and `GET /notes/search/suggest` MUST be registered BEFORE `GET /notes/:id` in Express router
+- Otherwise Express would match `search` as the `:id` parameter
+
+## What Done Looks Like
+
+- `npm test` passes all 35 tests (15 CRUD + 20 search)
+- All 14 search criteria above pass
+- All 3 sync criteria pass
+- All 4 suggest criteria pass
